# cfctl v2 reads NO credentials or configuration from env files.
# The v1 env-file contract (~/.config/cfctl/.env, CF_WORKSPACE_ENV_FILE,
# CF_TOKEN_LANE lanes, `cfctl env sources`) is retired — see
# docs/v1-parity.md. This file exists only to document that retirement so
# stale habits fail loudly here instead of silently in a shell.
#
# Credentials enter through governed import lanes and live in the platform
# keyring (macOS Keychain / Linux Secret Service), with a governed mode-0600
# file fallback under cfctl's state directory when the keyring is unusable.
# `cfctl doctor --json` reports the active secret-store backend.
#
#   printf '%s' "$CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN" | \
#     cfctl auth import-api-token --account <account-id> --stdin
#
#   # When piping through a build wrapper that consumes stdin (e.g. the
#   # ./cfctl cargo shim), pass a mode-0600 file instead:
#   cfctl auth import-api-token --account <account-id> --value-in <path>
#
# The complete environment surface the v2 binary reads:
#
#   CFCTL_HOME             absolute root overriding config/data/cache dirs
#   CFCTL_AGENT            configured local agent (codex|claude|cursor|gemini)
#   CFCTL_AGENT_SESSION    set by cfctl on launched agents; recursion guard
#   CFCTL_FORCE_IPV4       bind API egress to IPv4 (IPv4-allowlisted tokens)
#   CFCTL_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID  OAuth client id until public cfctl OAuth promotes
#
# Nothing below this line is read by cfctl. Do not add variables here.
